Idioms
description: compositions of the primitives - not new syntax
- 'The everyday questions are compositions of the primitives, never new syntax:'
- !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
  header:
    - Want
    - Query
      width: 3
  - ['members of onto O', '`O: -` - membership is a bookmark edge, so the filed materials and fragments are O''s own keyless members']
  - ['ontos of node N', '`: N: ?..: !!<format: x-yamlover-onto>` - memberships walked up; a fragment''s ontos likewise from the fragment member']
  - ['sub-ontos of O (not members)', '`O: ?: !!<*:: yamlover: $defs: onto>`']
  - ['all onto nodes (the picker)', '`:: ...: !!<format: x-yamlover-onto>`']
  - ['find-usages of N', '`N: ?..`']
  - ['every blob under here', '`...: !!<type: binary>`']
- >
  The future extensions - repetition and quantifiers, regex matching, branching, the capture sigil,
  projection - live behind the reserved characters (`! ( ) < > = |`), so none of them changes the
  meaning of a v1 query when it lands.
